  "wrapper_changes": "Remove provider autotune/heuristic decorators; preserve do_not_specialize=['T']; bind flags explicitly. Each variant independently tunes identical configurations.",
  "case_origin": "Exact kernel has upstream correctness tests at T=63/500/1000/1024/2048 and D=60/64/128, fp32/fp16/bf16, grouped heads, normalized QK and initial state. These are supported test inputs, not production-frequency evidence. Decode benchmark per-sequence length is1; our decode dimensions follow it but correct scalar-gating argument shapes.",
  "benchmark_caveat": "Pinned bench_fused_kda_decode's legacy3-kernel branch supplies per-channel gate/dt_bias to scalar-gating API and ignores returned recurrence output before RMSNorm. It is not used as a correctness or complete-block performance baseline. Speculative KDA benchmarks call another fused kernel, so short multi-token varlen cases here are diagnostics only.",
  "work_scope": "One complete scalar-gating recurrent operator: every timestep output plus final in-place state writes. Every timed invocation includes reset of state from identical snapshot. Does not include convolution or gated RMSNorm/model block.",
  "liger_correction": "Plain fast backward path already hoists scalar gradient; prior general-path plain specialization must not be treated as a production LICM opportunity.",
